  "suite": "greptile",
  "rule": "Exposure is counted per case, not per repository group: a golden comment read for one pull request contaminates that pull request. A case is exposed when its truth was read as a dossier, or when it is the same pull request (the same URL, or the same title on the pinned golden files) or the same base and head commits as a Martian case whose golden comments were read. Every exposed or unknown case is a tune case. The clean cases (exposure none), grouped by repository group and ordered by sha256(salt, NUL, group), are taken one at a time: a group joins tune while the score side keeps at least the floor without it, and stays on the score side otherwise. Tune cases are the development side, score cases the test side: a score run is a release run on the test split, logged in index/heldout-access.jsonl. The file is never rewritten: new exposure is a new split, which is a new file.",
  "note": "The floor of 20 score cases is a feasibility floor, not a claim of statistical adequacy: 20 cases give a wide interval on any rate.",
